{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-statistics","topic_code":"2.12","key":"A","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"A","ambiguous":false,"work":"The researcher calculates the mean of each sample of size n = 50 and plots these means, so each dot represents one sample mean. By the Central Limit Theorem, because the sample size n = 50 is sufficiently large (n >= 30), the sampling distribution of the sample mean is approximately normal regardless of the population's shape. The center of this distribution is the population mean mu = 28 minutes, and the standard deviation is sigma / sqrt(n) = 18 / sqrt(50) = 18 / (approx 7.07) approx 2.55 minutes, which is near 2.5 minutes."},"usage":{"inputTokens":385,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":385,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":556,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":163,"reasoningTokens":393},"totalTokens":941,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":393,"promptTokenCount":385,"candidatesTokenCount":163,"totalTokenCount":941,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":385}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":163}]},"reasoningTokens":393,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4594},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":14340,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":14340,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":1177,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":214,"reasoningTokens":963},"totalTokens":15517,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":963,"promptTokenCount":14340,"candidatesTokenCount":214,"totalTokenCount":15517,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality"