{"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","subject_key":"ap-statistics","topic_code":"2.12","key":"A","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"A","ambiguous":false,"work":"The dotplot is of the 1,000 sample means, not individual commute times. By the Central Limit Theorem, with sample size n=50, the sampling distribution of the sample mean is approximately normal even though the population is strongly right-skewed. Its center is the population mean, 28 minutes, and its standard deviation is sigma/sqrt(n) = 18/sqrt(50), which is approximately 2.5 minutes. Therefore, option A is correct."},"usage":{"inputTokens":439,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":439,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":516,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":118,"reasoningTokens":398},"totalTokens":955,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":439,"completion_tokens":516,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":439,"total_tokens":955,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":398}},"reasoningTokens":398,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4524},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":["Choice A is noticeably longer and more detailed than the distractors."]},"usage":{"inputTokens":13497,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":441,"cacheReadTokens":13056},"outputTokens":4631,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":197,"reasoningTokens":4434},"totalTokens":18128,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":13497,"completion_tokens":4631,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":13056,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":441,"total_tokens":18128,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":13056},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":