{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-statistics","topic_code":"3.12","key":"B","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"B","ambiguous":false,"work":"The planner suspects that the proportion of commuters who bike is greater in North City than South City, meaning the alternative hypothesis should reflect p1 > p2, or p1 - p2 > 0. The null hypothesis states no difference, so H0: p1 - p2 = 0. Hypotheses are always stated in terms of population parameters (p), not sample statistics (p-hat), eliminating D. The pooled proportion is calculated as (x1 + x2) / (n1 + n2) = (46 + 45) / (200 + 300) = 91 / 500 = 0.182. Thus, option B is correct."},"usage":{"inputTokens":424,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":424,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":459,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":176,"reasoningTokens":283},"totalTokens":883,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":283,"promptTokenCount":424,"candidatesTokenCount":176,"totalTokenCount":883,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":424}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":176}]},"reasoningTokens":283,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":4649},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":14442,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":14442,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":872,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":214,"reasoningTokens":658},"totalTokens":15314,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":658,"promptTokenCount":14442,"candidatesTokenCount":214,"totalTokenCount":15314,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":14442}],"candidatesTok