{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-statistics","topic_code":"3.15","key":"C","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"C","ambiguous":false,"work":"For a chi-square test of independence, the large counts condition requires all expected counts to be at least 5. Since the expected counts are 6, 24, 18, and 72, all are greater than or equal to 5, so the condition is satisfied. The contribution of each cell to the chi-square test statistic is calculated as (Observed - Expected)^2 / Expected. For the instrument/math-club cell, Observed = 10 and Expected = 6, yielding a contribution of (10 - 6)^2 / 6 = 16 / 6 ≈ 2.67. Thus, statement C is correct."},"usage":{"inputTokens":444,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":444,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":556,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":167,"reasoningTokens":389},"totalTokens":1000,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":389,"promptTokenCount":444,"candidatesTokenCount":167,"totalTokenCount":1000,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":444}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":167}]},"reasoningTokens":389,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5852},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":14395,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":14395,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":1062,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":214,"reasoningTokens":848},"totalTokens":15457,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":848,"promptTokenCount":14395,"candidatesTokenCount":214,"totalTokenCount":15457,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":14395}],