{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-statistics","topic_code":"3.6","key":"A","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"A","ambiguous":false,"work":"A p-value is the probability of obtaining a test statistic (or sample result) at least as extreme as the observed result, assuming that the null hypothesis is true. Here, the null hypothesis is that 30% of all customers order oat milk (p = 0.30), and the alternative is a right-tailed test (p > 0.30). Therefore, a p-value of 0.04 means that if 30% of all customers order oat milk, there is about a 4% chance that a random sample of this size would result in a sample proportion as large as or larger than the one observed. Option A correctly states this definition."},"usage":{"inputTokens":411,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":411,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":490,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":167,"reasoningTokens":323},"totalTokens":901,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":323,"promptTokenCount":411,"candidatesTokenCount":167,"totalTokenCount":901,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":411}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":167}]},"reasoningTokens":323,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5299},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":["Choice A is slightly longer than the distractors due to specifying both the conditional premise and sample size framing."]},"usage":{"inputTokens":14349,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":14349,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":698,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":241,"reasoningTokens":457},"totalTokens":15047,"raw":{"thoug